bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27, 0, "Pure-Simple compiler interpreter tables (src/compiler/10.frontend/core/interpreter/eval_tables.spl struct_table_register/struct_table_lookup, line 982/1000) key classes by BARE name with last-write-wins; two modules declaring the same class name collapse onto one decl id. test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/class_name_collision_warning_spec.spl pins last-write-wins as the warned behaviour. Owner decision 2026-11-27 (seed bug interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26): a class is identified by its owner module and an import alias is a local name for the owner-qualified class; the pure-Simple tables need the same owner keying."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "Pure-Simple interpreter class table keyed by bare name (last-write-wins)", src/compiler/10.frontend/core/interpreter/eval_tables.spl, 982, test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_owner_module_spec.spl, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27, 0, "2026-11-27 aarch64, seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-wr-seed1126b/release/simple (sha256 fb80903917d6d5f5) running the pure-Simple interpreter via core_interpret, base release/1.0.0 3f308bc4b31. Repro: pa.Thing + pb.Thing co-loaded, Thing.create().compile()*10000 + pb_make().compile() gave 10101010 (pb bodies for both) instead of 241010. Also missing on base, independent of the collision: `use m.{Solo as L}` (undefined variable L) and `m.Solo.create()` (undefined variable m) for a single-owner class. Pre-existing gaps NOT fixed here: same-module overload by param type (`fn show(n: i64)` beside `fn show(t: T)` -> type mismatch), struct destructuring patterns (`case P(x: x)` / `case P { x }`), `is` checks; display prints `T(...)`."
    pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27, 1, "2026-11-27 fix on work/purespl-same-name-class-20261127: owner-keyed struct table + struct_resolve_for_caller (own def, import binding route incl. alias, flat fallback); instances carry their struct decl; Type__method resolves in the declaring module for shared names. Red->green: same_name_class_owner_module_spec 1/11 -> 11/11, class_name_collision_warning_spec 2/4 -> 4/4. Scope: core interpreter only. HIR/MIR (50.mir module_lowering struct_owner_method_key) already key layouts as {module}::{Name}; native/self-hosted codegen of the alias/qualified cases is NOT verified here (needs a bootstrap deploy)."
    pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27, 2, "2026-11-27 follow-up: glob/whole-module imports now bind class names (extract_module_exports exports DECL_STRUCT when no explicit export list), trait impls dispatch per owner, and a caller with no route to a shared name gets a once-per-name [WARN] before the flat last-loaded pick. Known remaining gaps: an alias whose local name equals an unrelated single-owner class (`use m.{Foo as Widget}` beside a unique `Widget`) still builds the flat Widget; reflection builtins in eval_builtins.spl (struct_table_get_module, tr_* type lookups) stay flat; two glob imports of the same name bind the first."
    pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27, 3, "2026-11-27 review fixes: (1) top-level val/var initializers of the entry (eval_module Phase 2) and of imported modules (load_module init loop) now resolve with their own file as caller (eval_toplevel_owner) instead of module_get_path(), which was the last import; a top-level alias (val L0 = Legacy(n: 5)) now constructs. (2) struct_member_decl no longer borrows a member from ANOTHER same-named class when the owner lacks it (now not-found; a third module impl still dispatches). (3) register_module_functions registers classes before methods so the Type__method collision warning is skipped for owner-keyed shared class names. Red->green: same_name_class_owner_module_spec 14/18 -> 18/18 (new: entry top-level pa/pb and pb/pa order, top-level alias, missing-owner method, unrouted warning via struct_unrouted_warned). SIMPLE_LAZY_PARSE=1: base 4/18, head 6/18, no example green on base is red on head; under lazy parse an imported class is undefined variable on base too (pre-existing lazy loader gap, not this fix). Perf follow-up handed to Fable."

